---
title: "x_oracle_price_update - Multi-Oracle Price Verification (Scallop Lend)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_fetch_primary: fetch price from primary oracle (Pyth)
    q_fetch_primary --> q_check_primary: validate primary price is fresh
    q_check_primary --> q_error_stale: primary price is stale
    q_error_stale --> [*]: abort error (stale price)
    q_check_primary --> q_fetch_secondary: primary price is fresh
    q_fetch_secondary --> q_check_secondary: fetch price from secondary oracle (Supra)
    q_check_secondary --> q_compare: validate secondary price is fresh
    q_compare --> q_check_deviation: calc deviation = abs(primary - secondary) / primary
    q_check_deviation --> q_error_anomaly: deviation > threshold
    q_error_anomaly --> [*]: abort error (price anomaly detected)
    q_check_deviation --> q_apply_twap: deviation <= threshold
    q_apply_twap --> q_update: apply TWAP smoothing
    q_update --> [*]: update x_oracle price for asset

    note right of q_compare
        INV-001: primary oracle is Pyth, secondary is Supra
        INV-002: operation aborted if price anomaly detected between oracles
        INV-003: TWAP oracle provides time-weighted average to resist manipulation
    end note

    note right of q_fetch_primary
        INV-004: oracle price must be updated in same PTB before any price-dependent operation
        INV-005: oracle update incurs additional fee (less than 0.01 SUI)
        INV-006: price staleness check prevents using outdated prices
    end note
